      "claim": "Epimedin B was the least concentrated compound in rat brain and could hardly pass the blood-brain barrier, providing a contradictory example among the analogs.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Most structurally related molecules show detectable brain or CSF exposure after systemic administration, supporting meaningful CNS access. One analog is poorly brain-penetrant, but the overall experimental record favors a pass.",
